cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TransXplorer in your research, please cite the following work."
title: "TransXplorer: An automated translational discovery platform for RNA-seq data"
abstract: >
  TransXplorer is a free, no-login web platform that integrates the entire
  RNA-seq translational workflow — FASTQ processing, GEO import, automated
  batch-effect detection, differential expression, pathway enrichment, PPI
  networks with CytoHubba consensus hub detection, auto-optimized WGCNA,
  cell-type deconvolution, hybrid DoRothEA + TFLink regulatory network
  inference across 11 organisms, real-time DGIdb + OpenTargets drug-target
  mapping, and TCGA clinical validation across 33 cohorts — into a single
  R Shiny environment.
